# Badge

## Basic Usage

### Badge Variants

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="BadgeBadgeVariantsDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  import { ref } from 'vue'

  const initialCount = 8
  const count = ref(initialCount)
  const errorDot = ref(true)
  const resetDemo = () => {
    count.value = initialCount
    errorDot.value = true
  }
  </script>

  <template>
    <TxFlex direction="column" gap="16px">
      <TxFlex align="center" gap="12px" wrap="wrap">
        <TxBadge :value="count" />
        <TxBadge value="New" variant="primary" />
        <TxBadge value="99+" variant="success" />
        <TxBadge v-if="errorDot" dot variant="error" />
      </TxFlex>
      <TxFlex align="center" gap="8px" wrap="wrap">
        <TxButton size="sm" @click="count++">Add</TxButton>
        <TxButton size="sm" variant="secondary" :disabled="count === 0" @click="count--">Decrease</TxButton>
        <TxButton size="sm" variant="secondary" @click="resetDemo">Reset</TxButton>
        <TxSwitch v-model="errorDot" />
      </TxFlex>
    </TxFlex>
  </template>
---
:::

### Pop Motion

`open` drives the badge in and out: entering slides from the anchor offset with a scale/blur pop, closing pops out quickly while keeping the layout box. Numeric content renders through NumberFlow, so count changes roll per digit.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="BadgeBadgeMotionDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  import { ref } from 'vue'

  const open = ref(true)
  const count = ref(8)
  </script>

  <template>
    <span style="position: relative; display: inline-flex">
      <TxButton variant="secondary">Inbox</TxButton>
      <TxBadge variant="error" :value="count" :open="open" class="corner" />
    </span>
    <TxSwitch v-model="open" />
    <TxButton size="sm" round @click="count++">+1</TxButton>
  </template>

  <style scoped>
  .corner {
    position: absolute;
    top: -8px;
    right: -10px;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  </style>
---
:::

## Composition Examples

### Custom Slot Content

```vue
<template>
  <TxBadge variant="primary">
    <strong>Beta</strong>
  </TxBadge>
</template>
```

### Custom Color

```vue
<template>
  <TxBadge value="Internal" color="#111827" />
</template>
```

### Dot Indicator

```vue
<template>
  <TxFlex align="center" gap="8px">
    <TxBadge dot variant="error" />
    <span>Service degraded</span>
  </TxFlex>
</template>
```

## Interaction Contract

- The root is an inline `span` with pill styling.
- `variant` controls default CSS variables for background, text, and border colors.
- `color` overrides the background via `--tx-badge-bg` and forces `--tx-badge-text: #ffffff`.
- When `dot=true`, the component renders `.tx-badge__dot`, adds `tx-badge--dot`, and does not render `value` or default slot text.
- When `dot=false`, the default slot takes priority over `value`.
- `value` defaults to `0`, so an empty badge still renders `0` unless a slot or `dot` is used.
- Numeric `value` renders through NumberFlow and rolls per digit on change; strings and slot content render as-is.
- Toggling `open` plays the pop motion: entering slides in with a scale/blur pop, closing pops out quickly while keeping the layout box; the entrance never plays on first mount.
- Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` the pop motion is disabled, and NumberFlow honors the same preference.
- `TxBadge` has no click event, positioning logic, overflow truncation, or target anchoring behavior.

## API

### Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `variant` | `'default' \| 'primary' \| 'success' \| 'warning' \| 'error'` | `'default'` | Color preset. |
| `value` | `number \| string` | `0` | Badge text content when the default slot is not used and `dot=false`. |
| `color` | `string` | - | Custom background color. Also sets text color to white. |
| `dot` | `boolean` | `false` | Render a compact dot and hide text content. |
| `open` | `boolean` | `true` | Presence switch; toggling plays the slide/pop motion, and the closed badge keeps its layout box. |

### Events

`TxBadge` does not emit component events. Attach interactions to surrounding controls when a badge needs to behave like a filter or notification target.

### Slots

| Slot | Props | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `default` | - | Custom pill content. Ignored when `dot=true`. |

### CSS Variables

| Variable | Source | Description |
|----------|--------|-------------|
| `--tx-badge-bg` | `variant` / `color` | Badge background. |
| `--tx-badge-text` | `variant` / `color` | Badge text color. |
| `--tx-badge-border` | `variant` | Badge border color. |
| `--tx-badge-offset-x` / `--tx-badge-offset-y` | optional consumer hook | Slide-in start offset, defaults `-8.2px` / `12.4px`. |
| `--tx-badge-slide-dur` | optional consumer hook | Slide-in duration, default `260ms`. |
| `--tx-badge-pop-dur` / `--tx-badge-pop-close-dur` | optional consumer hook | Open/close scale+blur durations, defaults `500ms` / `180ms`. |
| `--tx-badge-fade-dur` / `--tx-badge-fade-close-dur` | optional consumer hook | Fade durations, defaults `400ms` / `180ms`. |
| `--tx-badge-blur` | optional consumer hook | Closed-state blur amount, default `2px`. |
| `--tx-badge-slide-ease` / `--tx-badge-pop-ease` / `--tx-badge-close-ease` | optional consumer hook | Easing curves of the three motion phases. |

## Best Practices

- Use `TxBadge` for counts and small state hints. Use `TxStatusBadge` when the label needs a status icon or permission mapping.
- Keep badge text short; `white-space: nowrap` prevents wrapping.
- For target-corner notification badges, position `TxBadge` in the host component. `TxBadge` does not anchor itself.
- Do not rely on dot color alone for critical states; pair dot indicators with adjacent text.
- Prefer variants for semantic states and reserve `color` for brand or custom taxonomy labels.
- For corner notifications, bind `open` to the unread state and let the pop motion handle appearance; do not stack your own transform on the badge.

